{"book":{"id":"book-ogallala-water-for-a-dry-land-john-opie","slug":"ogallala-water-for-a-dry-land-john-opie","title":"Ogallala: Water for a Dry Land","authors":[{"id":"person-john-opie","name":"John Opie"}],"isbn13":["9780803235571"],"subjects":["History"],"topics":["Oceans, Rivers & Water","Energy, Extraction & Resources","Essays & Cultural Criticism","Food, Agriculture & Land"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Ogallala%3A%20Water%20for%20a%20Dry%20Land%20John%20Opie","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Ogallala%3A%20Water%20for%20a%20Dry%20Land%20John%20Opie","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Ogallala%3A%20Water%20for%20a%20Dry%20Land%20John%20Opie","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Ogallala%3A%20Water%20for%20a%20Dry%20Land%20John%20Opie","publisher":"https://books.google.com/books/about/Ogallala.html?hl=&id=TbH1dYAT2eQC"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-george-perkins-marsh-environmental-history-american-society-for-environmental-history-official-p","source-google-books-ogallala-water-for-a-dry-land-john-opie","source-open-library-ogallala-water-for-a-dry-land-john-opie","source-cover-open-library-ogallala-water-for-a-dry-land-john-opie"],"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"History","sourceId":"source-google-books-ogallala-water-for-a-dry-land-john-opie"}],"publicationYear":1993,"pageCount":440,"summary":"The Ogallala aquifer, a vast store of underground water reserves extending from South Dakota through Texas, is the product of eons of accumulated glacial melts, ancient Rocky Mountain snow melts, and rainfall, all percolating slowly through gravel beds hundreds of feet thick. Irrigation from the aquifer has allowed the High Plains region to prosper, but without revolutionary changes in the management of this resource, the future may bring a return to subsistence conditions. Focusing on the Ogallala aquifer, John Opie vividl